#!/usr/bin/env python3
from common import fail
'Portable rework brief. See the openproblem README for inputs.'
from common import BUILD_SCOPE, Context, REPO, entry

def main(argv):
    ctx = Context()
    import sys, json, pathlib
    S = ctx.scratch
    sp = json.load(open(argv[1]))
    _prior = sorted((p.name for p in (S / 'lanes').glob(f"rework-{sp['lane']}*.json") if p.resolve() != pathlib.Path(argv[1]).resolve()))
    if len(_prior) >= 2 and (not sp.get('mathematical_defect')):
        fail(13, f"""REDO_LIMIT lane {sp['lane']}: {len(_prior)} prior redo specs {_prior}; CLAUDE.md §3.6 ④ stops the lane at the third non-mathematical redo. Set "mathematical_defect": "<the mathematical finding>" in the spec only when the redo fixes mathematics.""")
    goal = (S / 'briefs/goal-artifact.yaml').read_text()
    lb = ctx.block('lean-report-block.md').read_text()
    rows = '\n'.join(sp['standing_rows'])
    t = f"""# sshx implementation-seat brief — lane `op-{sp['lane']}` — rework PR #{sp['pr']} after review round findings (module change, so the candidate's own freeze is redone)\n\n{BUILD_SCOPE}\n\nYou are one codex-cli implementation seat. Work only in the worktree below. Commit messages and files carry no session links.\n\n## GoalArtifact (complete; cite in visible_inputs)\n```yaml\n{goal.rstrip()}\n```\n\n## Worktree and state\n`{sp['worktree']}`, branch `{sp['branch']}`, PR #{sp['pr']} (open), head `{sp['head']}`. `git status --short` must be empty and `git rev-parse HEAD` must equal that SHA before you start; otherwise stop and report `open` with the readings. Toolchain: `eval "$(sed -n '/^export PATH=/p' tools/scripts/local-harness-gate.sh)"`, `make -C tools dotnet` once. Follow `skills/codex-formalize/SKILL.md` Steps 5–8 and `CLAUDE.md` §3.2 (every private theorem/lemma is genuine content or inlined as a `have`; open-problem-resolution conditions (a)–(d)); judge by bare exit codes.\n\n## Findings to fix (from the review round; verified by the orchestrator)\n{sp['fixes']}\n\n## Procedure\n1. **Rebuild the branch from fresh `origin/dev` (CLAUDE.md §4.7: a frozen candidate is repaired by abandoning the branch and redoing the deposit; never hand-edit `Golden/**`).** Let `H` be the head above. `git fetch origin dev`; `git switch -C rebuild-{sp['lane']} origin/dev`. Bring over ONLY the lane's non-ledger files from `H` with `git show H:<path> > <path>` (create directories as needed): the module `.lean`, its `.scribe.cs` and `.md`, the Library note, the `Problems/` dossier(s) (and the lane's `Reg/D5/**` mirror if one exists; see the escape-audit block) — list them with `git diff --name-only origin/dev...H -- D5 Blueprint Library Problems` and exclude any path that is not this lane's (e.g. another module's projection). Never copy anything under `Golden/`. The new branch carries no freeze of this module until the door runs.\n2. **Phase A.** Apply the module/Scribe fixes above. Temporarily remove every `OpenProblemResolutionClaim` node from the Scribe and move the `Problems/` dossier(s) of this PR aside (`/tmp/op-{sp['lane']}/`). `make lean LEAN_TARGETS="<the delivered modules and every frozen module you re-pin, dotted>"` EXIT=0 (the build lock is shared by every worktree); direct `/usr/bin/time -l lake env lean {sp['module']}.lean` EXIT=0 (report wall seconds and maximum resident set size); `#print axioms` on every public declaration = the three standard axioms; `tools/scripts/agent/header-check.sh {sp['module']}.lean` EXIT=0; `make lean-report-scoped LEAN_TARGETS="<the same list>"` EXIT=0 (the build lock is shared by every worktree); `make emit` EXIT=0 and a rerun reports 0 changed. Commit (subject `{sp['commit_source']}`).\n3. **Door**, in ONE command: `git fetch origin && git merge --no-edit origin/dev && B="$(git merge-base HEAD origin/dev)" && make deposit-uncovered GID={sp['gid']} BASE="$B"` (`origin/dev` is shared by every worktree and moves while other seats fetch, so pass the SHA this tree merged, never the moving ref; freshness against the latest dev is the CI merge-tree check) EXIT=0 (on `LEDGER_ALIGN_FAILED`/`dependency-not-ready`: stop, report `open`, no hand edits).\n4. **Phase B.** Restore the resolution-claim node(s) and the dossier(s); apply any dossier/Library fixes above; `make emit` EXIT=0 and a rerun reports 0 changed; the Scribe suites that render the document EXIT=0; Skip the local full gate and list it under `not_run`; the doors choose their own scope and the required CI check supplies the full gate. ONE builder commit (subject `{sp['commit_builder']}`) with the new Freeze event, state pin, dossier(s) and re-emitted mirror. Late dedupe on fresh `origin/dev`. Publish without a force push (CLAUDE.md §6.1): keep the reviewed remote head `{sp['head']}` as an ancestor. On the rebuilt branch run `git merge -s ours --no-edit {sp['head']}`; this records `{sp['head']}` as the second parent and keeps the rebuilt tree, so `git diff --quiet HEAD^1 HEAD` must exit 0. Then `git branch -f {sp['branch']} HEAD && git switch {sp['branch']} && LEAN4_GUARDRAILS_BYPASS=1 git push origin {sp['branch']}` (a fast-forward; never `--force` or `--force-with-lease`). Verify with `git ls-remote` that the remote head is your final commit, and with `git merge-base --is-ancestor {sp['head']} HEAD` that the reviewed head is an ancestor. (The PR keeps its number.)\n4′. **Foreign projections and registration.** `git diff --name-only origin/dev...HEAD -- Blueprint` must name only this module's `.scribe.cs`/`.md`; restore any other path to the exact `origin/dev` bytes before the builder commit. The escape audit follows the escape-audit block below (CLAUDE.md §3.9): exempt refutation results say so in one sentence; other public theorems carry a registration attempt or a linked unfinished-audit issue; nothing says registration is "paused".\n5. **PR body** (`gh pr view {sp['pr']} --json body -q .body > /tmp/op-{sp['lane']}/body.md`, edit, `gh pr edit {sp['pr']} --body-file …`): re-take every Verification reading at the new head (one row per reading; `make emit` is one row); update the escape table and the module state record (path and `statement_id`); apply the body fixes above; delete any `Freeze order:` / `Production order:` sentence or other implementation sequence (CLAUDE.md §2.10: reviewers reject them as process narration); name the independent judgement-form reviewer once, in the carriers-and-roles provenance, as `Independent judgement-form and mirror reviewer (producer of the proof_shape classification above): codex-cli seat <id>`. In the standing section keep all existing table rows (if it still holds the first-publication sentence `Round 1 seat layout at … No round has completed …`, delete that sentence) and append:\n{rows}\nthen the line `{sp['tally_line']}` and, as the last standing line, `{sp['next_layout_line']}` with `HEAD` replaced by your final commit. No process narrative (CLAUDE.md §2.10): describe the delivery as it now is. `python3 tools/scripts/agent/openproblem/standing-check.py {sp['pr']} --round {sp['next_round']}` must print `STANDING_CHECK findings=0`.\n6. `make pr-watch PR={sp['pr']} HEAD_SHA=<final head>` last; report the `PR_WATCH_RESULT` line.\n\n{lb}\n\n## Result envelope\n`conclusion` = {{"verdict":"success|open","pr_number":{sp['pr']},"head":"…","state_record":{{"path":"…","statement_id":"…"}},"exit_codes":{{…}},"print_axioms":{{…}},"direct_lean_seconds":…,"peak_rss_bytes":…,"fixes_applied":[…],"standing_check":"…","pr_watch_result":"…","assumed_unverified":[…],"open_reasons":[…],"visible_inputs":["GoalArtifact(complete)","review findings","worktree files"]}}, plus `log_ref`.\n"""
    out = S / 'briefs' / f"rework-{sp['lane']}.md"
    extra =  ctx.block('escape-audit-block.md').read_text() + ctx.block('reuse-sweep-block.md').read_text() + ctx.block('no-preflight-block.md').read_text() + ctx.block('frozen-state-contract-block.md').read_text() + ctx.block('stageb-body-rules-block.md').read_text() + ctx.block('actions-cache-block.md').read_text().replace('<PR>', str(sp['pr'])) + ctx.block('scoped-doors-block.md').read_text() + ctx.block('dossier-sections-block.md').read_text() + '\n' + ctx.block('ci-gate-block.md').read_text() + ctx.block('rework-mirror-block.md').read_text() + '\n' + ctx.block('stagea-scribe-build-block.md').read_text()
    out.write_text(t + extra)
    print(out, len(t))

if __name__ == '__main__':
    import sys
    sys.exit(entry(main, minimum=1, maximum=1))
